  "limitations": [
    "Internal author review is not independent editorial approval.",
    "Seven documented contracts: filesystem append concurrency, S3 signed upload, symlink target, Redis flush scope, named pool results, Vite environment exposure and browser Fetch credentials.",
    "Runtime cache/lock fixtures use deterministic single-process witnesses; no distributed race benchmark or shared Redis service was executed.",
    "Q445 verifies configured timeout options, not elapsed network behavior; Q488 compares generated SQL, not actual PostgreSQL lock contention.",
    "HTTP fakes run the actual Laravel client middleware with a terminal transport that always refuses network access; pool concurrency remains a source contract.",
    "Inertia tests exercise the PHP server adapter, not a mounted React/Vue client or an SSR service.",
    "Local Vite manifest fixtures verify Laravel asset resolution; no real frontend bundle build is claimed.",
    "PHPUnit assertion helpers and Laravel feature request traits execute directly in isolated fixtures; these are not claims of running a complete project PHPUnit suite.",
    "Final 600-question cross-review and review-app/browser regressions remain outstanding."
  ],
